The photo shows a small pile of mixed salad greens on a square plate about 26 cm wide. The greens cover roughly 10 by 12 cm and look loosely piled and light. A pile like that probably weighs 35-45 g, so I'll use 40 g.

Salad greens run about 20 kcal per 100 g, which is only about 8 kcal for 40 g. There may be a little dressing, since the leaves look slightly glossy, so I'll add about 25 kcal for it. That brings the total to roughly 30 kcal.

